    "index.html": {
      "text": [
        "zer0-mistakes remote theme",
        "Welcome — your site is live!",
        "GitHub Pages built this page from just three files in your repository. The layout, styles, and this entire onboarding screen are served by the remote theme.",
        "Use the wizard below to generate a personalised _config.yml, drop it into your repo, and your site will look like your site instead of this welcome page.",
        "Start the wizard Minimal starter",
        "Your repository right now",
        "_config.yml required",
        "Gemfile required",
        "index.md required",
        "pages/ optional",
        "assets/ optional",
        "Everything else — layouts, styles, navigation, search — is provided by the remote theme.",
        "The 3-file starter",
        "The only files you need in your repository for GitHub Pages to render a full site through the bamr87/zer0-mistakes remote theme.",
        "The minimum viable configuration:",
        "# _config.yml title: \"My Site\" description: \"A site rendered by the zer0-mistakes remote theme.\" url: \"\" baseurl: \"\" # Pull layouts/includes/assets from the published theme remote_theme: bamr87/zer0-mistakes # GitHub Pages whitelisted plugins plugins: - jekyll-remote-theme - jekyll-feed - jekyll-sitemap - jekyll-seo-tag # Hide this welcome screen once you're configured site_configured: true",
        "Use the wizard below to generate a richer file with collections, analytics, and social links.",
        "Required when building locally; GitHub Pages installs these for you in CI.",
        "# Gemfile source \"https://rubygems.org\" gem \"github-pages\", group: :jekyll_plugins gem \"jekyll-remote-theme\" gem \"webrick\", \"~> 1.7\"",
        "While the site is unconfigured, layout: welcome shows this onboarding screen. Once you set site_configured: true in _config.yml, the same file renders your own home-page content.",
        "--- layout: welcome title: Home --- # Welcome to my site Replace this with your own content. The setup wizard will disappear automatically once `site_configured: true` is set in `_config.yml`.",
        "Local development? Run bundle install && bundle exec jekyll serve (or docker compose up if you have a docker-compose.yml). Browse to http://localhost:4000/.",
        "Step 1 of 0",
        "Connect your AI",
        "The builder runs entirely in your browser. Connect Claude or Grok through the local dev proxy with your own token and it can fill in these forms, check your machine, read the theme's source, write or modify your project, generate images and start Docker — in the order you choose.",
        "Looking for the dev proxy…",
        "Checking",
        "AI provider",
        "Token for Claude",
        "Mint one with claude setup-token. The token goes once to the local proxy and stays in its memory — never in this page or your browser storage.",
        "Also save it to .env (mode 600) so the proxy remembers it next time",
        "Model claude-opus-5-5",
        "Sent with every request; the proxy can pin one with CHAT_MODEL / XAI_CHAT_MODEL.",
        "Image generation Off",
        "Renders hero, logo and post images straight into the project's assets/.",
        "How do you want to work?",
        "How to connect (once, on your machine)",
        "1",
        "Start the dev proxy next to the site",
        "Node 20.6+. It starts without any key and waits for the token you paste above; --env-file=.env loads keys you saved earlier.",
        "node --env-file=.env templates/deploy/chat-proxy/dev-proxy.mjs",
        "2",
        "Get a token from the provider you picked",
        "Claude: a personal OAuth token from the Claude Code CLI (Pro/Max) or an API key from console.anthropic.com. Grok: an API key from console.x.ai.",
        "claude setup-token",
        "3",
        "Paste it above — or keep it in .env",
        "Pasting keeps the token in the proxy's memory for this run (tick the switch to save it). Or put it in the git-ignored .env yourself and restart the proxy.",
        "CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-… # or XAI_API_KEY=xai-…",
        "What the proxy is allowed to do",
        "Hold the token you paste in memory only; write it to .env (mode 600) only when you tick the switch; report it masked.",
        "Run a fixed list of read-only version checks (Docker, Git, gh, VS Code, Node, Claude CLI).",
        "Read text source files inside the theme checkout — never .env, keys or build output.",
        "Write generated files into a folder beside the theme (never inside it), and read, edit, add or delete text files inside a site you open there — each change behind a confirmation card.",
        "Save generated images (PNG/JPEG/WebP only) under that site's assets/.",
        "Run docker compose up / ps / logs / down / build and git status / diff / log / init in that folder — nothing else.",
        "No proxy? Continue anyway. Every step still works and the Build step gives you the files and the commands to run yourself.",
        "Prerequisites",
        "Docker runs Jekyll for you, Git and the GitHub CLI publish it. Connected? Press Run checks. Otherwise tick each item as you install it.",
        "macOS Windows Linux",
        "0 of 0 required ready",
        "On macOS you can install everything at once: brew install git gh node && brew install --cask docker visual-studio-code Full guide: Machine Setup.",
        "Site identity",
        "Describe the site in your own words first — the assistant uses that brief to draft everything else.",
        "What is this site about, and who is it for?",
        "The brief is not published; it steers the drafts.",
        "Site title *",
        "Shown in the navbar, browser tab and feed.",
        "Subtitle (optional)",
        "Tagline (optional)",
        "Description",
        "Meta description for search and social cards. Aim for 120–160 characters. 0/160",
        "Author / owner",
        "Contact email",
        "GitHub & URLs",
        "Where the code lives and where the site is served from.",
        "GitHub username",
        "Repository name",
        "Also the project folder name in the Build step.",
        "How will the theme be loaded?",
        "Site URL",
        "Base path",
        "Empty for user.github.io; /repo for project sites.",
        "Permalink style /:categories/:title/ /:title/ /:year/:month/:title/ pretty",
        "Dev port",
        "Remote theme",
        "Structure",
        "Pick a starting shape, then fine-tune the collections and the top navigation.",
        "Kind of site",
        "Collections",
        "Navigation style",
        "Sidebar",
        "Landing page",
        "Example pages 0",
        "Each row becomes a real file with front matter. Bodies come from the assistant, or are drafted from the title.",
        "Main navigation",
        "Appearance",
        "Seven skins re-colour every component and background layer. Preview any of them on this page.",
        "Skin",
        "Applies theme_skin in _config.yml.",
        "Colour mode",
        "Lock the colour mode (hide the toggle)",
        "SVG background layers (gradient, pattern, noise)",
        "Palette layered over the skin",
        "Custom",
        "Primary",
        "Secondary",
        "Accent",
        "Fonts",
        "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. Headline weight.",
        "Corners",
        "Navbar icon (Bootstrap icon name)",
        "Voice & first content",
        "Set the tone, then let the assistant draft the welcome post and about page — or write them yourself.",
        "Tone",
        "Audience",
        "Welcome post title",
        "Welcome post body (Markdown)",
        "About page (Markdown)",
